READ THIS BEFORE THE TABLE.

README 5.2: arm c mixes implementation and runtime by construction, so its
number STANDS ALONE and is never quoted as a ratio against arm a. The
absolutes below are Mono absolutes and nothing else.

The one ratio arm c may legitimately carry is the one formed INSIDE its own
process: managed against Google.Protobuf, both on Mono. That answers a
question arm b cannot -- whether the design still wins where a pinned
consumer actually runs -- without comparing two runtimes.

It passes the SAME 120 correctness checks as arms a and b (below), which is
README 5.1's binding condition: identical wire bytes at every level.

